# High-water-mark state for the generic SQL-source connector (handoff 0033).
# The connector persists one small JSON file per adapter label here
# (sqlsource-<label>.json) recording the last warehouse key it has read, so
# a restart resumes instead of re-reading history. Deleting a state file is
# safe but should be DELIBERATE: the connector then re-reads the view from
# the beginning, which is idempotent (identical batches land identical
# content-addressed record ids; mapped rows carry deterministic natural
# keys) — it just costs one full re-read.
#
# Agency operational state, never source: nothing in here is committed.
#
# THIS .gitignore IS TRACKED ON PURPOSE, so the directory exists in every
# checkout. Without it, Docker creates the bind-mount path itself on first
# `up` — owned by ROOT — and the connector cannot write its state for
# reasons that have nothing to do with the person running it. (Same lesson
# as the 2026-07-28 nginx file-mode incident: never let a host permission
# accident decide whether the product works.)
*
!.gitignore
